{
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "title": "1. Overview",
      "text": "%md\n## 1. Overview\n\n### Checkpoint policy (#85)\n\nCheckpoint ID `streaming-gh-archive-file-v1` is owned by **Streaming Data Engineering Education** and classified as **generation reproducibility** state. Its concrete leaf binds the exact resolver generation by scale, publication ID, and manifest SHA-256. While active or uncertain it is retained; a completed or stopped leaf waits 14 days. Recovery must re-resolve that exact resolver generation and reset `lakehouse.bronze.gh_events_stream` before replay. Manual exact-leaf retention is available through issue #86's reviewed plan/prepare/apply protocol. Automated and scheduled deletion remain disabled pending stronger MinIO cross-process CAS and conditional delete proof.",
      "config": {},
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Setup",
      "text": "%md\n## 2. Setup",
      "config": {},
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Setup (code)",
      "text": "%spark\nimport spark.implicits._\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.functions._\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.types._\n// spark is pre-bound by the Atlas Zeppelin interpreter\nimport java.net.{HttpURLConnection, URL}\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets\nimport com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonParser\nimport com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.{JsonNode, ObjectMapper}\nimport scala.collection.JavaConverters._\n\nval datasetScaleOverride = Option(z.input(\"dataset_scale\", null))\nval datasetScale = datasetScaleOverride.orElse(Option(System.getenv(\"DATASET_SCALE\"))).getOrElse(\"small\")\nrequire(Set(\"tiny\", \"small\", \"medium\").contains(datasetScale), \"invalid DATASET_SCALE\")\nval resolverUri = Option(System.getenv(\"DATASET_RESOLVER_URI\")).getOrElse(throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"DATASET_RESOLVER_URI is required\"))\nval resolverConnection = new URL(resolverUri.stripSuffix(\"/\") + \"/v1/resolve\").openConnection().asInstanceOf[HttpURLConnection]\nresolverConnection.setRequestMethod(\"POST\")\nresolverConnection.setRequestProperty(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\nresolverConnection.setDoOutput(true)\nresolverConnection.setConnectTimeout(30000)\nresolverConnection.setReadTimeout(30000)\nval resolverRequest = \"{\\\"dataset\\\":\\\"gh_archive\\\",\\\"expected_scale\\\":\\\"\" + datasetScale + \"\\\"}\"\nval resolverOutput = resolverConnection.getOutputStream\nresolverOutput.write(resolverRequest.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8))\nresolverOutput.close()\nrequire(resolverConnection.getResponseCode == 200, \"dataset resolution failed\")\nval resolutionBytes = resolverConnection.getInputStream.readNBytes((1 << 20) + 1)\nrequire(resolutionBytes.length <= (1 << 20), \"dataset resolution failed\")\nval mapper = new ObjectMapper().enable(JsonParser.Feature.STRICT_DUPLICATE_DETECTION)\nval datasetResolution = mapper.readTree(resolutionBytes)\ndef jsonDepth(node: JsonNode): Int =\n  if (node.isContainerNode) 1 + node.elements.asScala.map(jsonDepth).foldLeft(0)(math.max) else 0\nrequire(jsonDepth(datasetResolution) <= 16, \"dataset resolution failed\")\nresolverConnection.disconnect()\nval datasetResolutionFields = Set(\"dataset\", \"scale\", \"plan_id\", \"manifest_sha256\", \"publication_id\", \"objects\")\nrequire(datasetResolution.fieldNames.asScala.toSet == datasetResolutionFields)\nrequire(\n  datasetResolution.get(\"dataset\").isTextual && datasetResolution.get(\"scale\").isTextual &&\n  datasetResolution.get(\"plan_id\").isTextual && datasetResolution.get(\"publication_id\").isTextual &&\n  datasetResolution.get(\"manifest_sha256\").isTextual,\n  \"dataset resolution failed\"\n)\nrequire(datasetResolution.get(\"dataset\").asText == \"gh_archive\" && datasetResolution.get(\"scale\").asText == datasetScale)\nval planId = datasetResolution.get(\"plan_id\").asText\nval publicationId = datasetResolution.get(\"publication_id\").asText\nval manifestSha256 = datasetResolution.get(\"manifest_sha256\").asText\nrequire(planId.matches(\"[0-9a-f]{64}\") && publicationId.matches(\"[0-9a-f]{12}4[0-9a-f]{3}[89ab][0-9a-f]{15}\") && manifestSha256.matches(\"[0-9a-f]{64}\"))\nval objectsNode = datasetResolution.get(\"objects\")\nrequire(objectsNode.isArray && objectsNode.size > 0, \"dataset resolution failed\")\nval datasetObjects = objectsNode.elements.asScala.toVector\nval datasetObjectFields = Set(\"object_name\", \"uri\", \"size_bytes\", \"sha256\", \"schema_id\")\nrequire(datasetObjects.forall { item =>\n  item.fieldNames.asScala.toSet == datasetObjectFields &&\n  item.get(\"object_name\").isTextual && item.get(\"object_name\").asText.matches(\"[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\") &&\n  !Set(\".\", \"..\").contains(item.get(\"object_name\").asText) && item.get(\"uri\").isTextual &&\n  item.get(\"size_bytes\").isIntegralNumber && item.get(\"size_bytes\").asLong >= 0 &&\n  item.get(\"sha256\").isTextual && item.get(\"sha256\").asText.matches(\"[0-9a-f]{64}\") && item.get(\"schema_id\").isTextual && item.get(\"schema_id\").asText.nonEmpty\n})\nval datasetObjectNames = datasetObjects.map(_.get(\"object_name\").asText)\nval expectedNamesByScale = Map(\n  \"tiny\" -> Vector(\"2023-01-01-0.json.gz\"),\n  \"small\" -> Vector(\"2023-01-01-0.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-1.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-2.json.gz\"),\n  \"medium\" -> Vector(\"2023-01-01-0.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-1.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-2.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-3.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-4.json.gz\", \"2023-01-01-5.json.gz\")\n)\nrequire(datasetObjectNames == expectedNamesByScale(datasetScale) && datasetObjectNames.distinct.size == datasetObjectNames.size)\nval datasetUris = datasetObjects.map(_.get(\"uri\").asText)\nval generationPrefix = s\"s3://landing/gh_archive/_generations/$planId/$publicationId/\"\nrequire(datasetUris.zip(datasetObjectNames).forall { case (uri, name) => uri == generationPrefix + name })\nval datasetSparkUris = datasetUris.map(uri => \"s3a://\" + uri.stripPrefix(\"s3://\"))\nval datasetObjectByName = datasetObjectNames.zip(datasetSparkUris).toMap",
      "config": {},
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "2. Checkpoint lease (code)",
      "text": "%spark\nimport java.net.{HttpURLConnection, URL}\nimport java.nio.charset.StandardCharsets\nimport java.util.UUID\nimport java.util.concurrent.{Executors, TimeUnit}\nimport java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicReference\nimport com.fasterxml.jackson.core.JsonParser\nimport com.fasterxml.jackson.databind.{JsonNode, ObjectMapper}\nimport org.apache.spark.sql.streaming.StreamingQuery\nimport scala.collection.JavaConverters._\n\nfinal class CheckpointLease(\n  checkpointId: String,\n  prefix: String,\n  workload: String,\n  terminalState: String,\n  generation: Map[String, String]\n) extends AutoCloseable {\n  private val origin = \"http://checkpoint-retention:8080\"\n  private val token = Option(System.getenv(\"CHECKPOINT_RETENTION_LEASE_TOKEN\"))\n    .filter(value => value.nonEmpty && value.getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8).length <= 256)\n    .getOrElse(throw new IllegalStateException(\"checkpoint lease configuration invalid\"))\n  private val leaseMapper = new ObjectMapper().enable(JsonParser.Feature.STRICT_DUPLICATE_DETECTION)\n  private val sessionId = UUID.randomUUID().toString\n  @volatile private var query: StreamingQuery = _\n  private val heartbeatFailure = new AtomicReference[Throwable]()\n  private val executor = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor { runnable =>\n    val thread = new Thread(runnable, \"checkpoint-lease\")\n    thread.setDaemon(true)\n    thread\n  }\n\n  private def post(path: String, value: JsonNode): JsonNode = {\n    val body = leaseMapper.writeValueAsBytes(value)\n    require(body.nonEmpty && body.length <= 65536, \"checkpoint lease request invalid\")\n    val connection = new URL(origin + path).openConnection().asInstanceOf[HttpURLConnection]\n    connection.setInstanceFollowRedirects(false)\n    connection.setRequestMethod(\"POST\")\n    connection.setRequestProperty(\"Authorization\", \"Bearer \" + token)\n    connection.setRequestProperty(\"Content-Type\", \"application/json\")\n    connection.setFixedLengthStreamingMode(body.length)\n    connection.setConnectTimeout(5000)\n    connection.setReadTimeout(10000)\n    connection.setDoOutput(true)\n    try {\n      val output = connection.getOutputStream\n      try output.write(body) finally output.close()\n      require(connection.getResponseCode == 200, \"checkpoint lease request failed\")\n      val input = connection.getInputStream\n      val responseBytes = try input.readNBytes(65537) finally input.close()\n      require(responseBytes.length <= 65536, \"checkpoint lease response invalid\")\n      leaseMapper.readTree(responseBytes)\n    } finally connection.disconnect()\n  }\n\n  private val epoch = {\n    val request = leaseMapper.createObjectNode()\n    request.put(\"checkpoint_id\", checkpointId)\n    request.put(\"owner_id\", \"zeppelin-notebook\")\n    request.put(\"prefix\", prefix)\n    request.put(\"session_id\", sessionId)\n    request.put(\"workload\", workload)\n    val value = post(\"/v1/leases/acquire\", request).path(\"epoch\").asText(\"\")\n    require(value.matches(\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[1-5][0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}\"), \"checkpoint lease response invalid\")\n    value\n  }\n\n  private def heartbeat(): Unit = {\n    val request = leaseMapper.createObjectNode()\n    request.put(\"checkpoint_id\", checkpointId)\n    request.put(\"epoch\", epoch)\n    request.put(\"prefix\", prefix)\n    post(\"/v1/leases/heartbeat\", request)\n  }\n\n  def bindQuery(value: StreamingQuery): Unit = {\n    require(value != null && query == null, \"checkpoint query invalid\")\n    query = value\n    executor.scheduleAtFixedRate(\n      new Runnable {\n        override def run(): Unit = {\n          try heartbeat()\n          catch {\n            case _: Throwable =>\n              heartbeatFailure.compareAndSet(null, new IllegalStateException(\"checkpoint heartbeat failed\"))\n              try if (query != null && query.isActive) query.stop() catch { case _: Throwable => () }\n          }\n        }\n      },\n      60,\n      60,\n      TimeUnit.SECONDS\n    )\n  }\n\n  override def close(): Unit = {\n    executor.shutdownNow()\n    if (query != null && query.isActive) query.stop()\n    heartbeat()\n    val request = leaseMapper.createObjectNode()\n    request.put(\"checkpoint_id\", checkpointId)\n    request.put(\"epoch\", epoch)\n    request.put(\"prefix\", prefix)\n    request.put(\"state\", terminalState)\n    val evidence = request.putObject(\"evidence\")\n    val generationNode = evidence.putObject(\"generation\")\n    generation.toSeq.sortBy(_._1).foreach { case (key, value) => generationNode.put(key, value) }\n    post(\"/v1/leases/terminal\", request)\n    Option(heartbeatFailure.get()).foreach(throw _)\n  }\n}",
      "config": {},
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "3. Read",
      "text": "%md\n## 3. Read",
      "config": {},
      "settings": {
        "params": {},
        "forms": {}
